# ============================================================================
# Die Dapper Klein Pikkewyn — English (canonical string table)
#
# TRANSLATING: copy this file to <code>.lang (e.g. af.lang, zh.lang) in this
# directory, translate the values, and select the language in-game with
# StringsSetLanguage("<code>"). Any key you leave out falls back to the
# English line, so partial translations are safe.
#
# Format: key = value          (one line per string, UTF-8)
#   - '#' starts a comment; blank lines are ignored
#   - '\n' in a value becomes a line break
#   - %s / %d are runtime placeholders — KEEP them, in the same order
#   - Numbered keys (.1 .2 .3 ...) are the pages of one conversation; a
#     translation may use fewer or more pages, numbering must stay contiguous
#   - Keep each value under ~200 characters — longer text overflows the
#     dialogue panel
# ============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tutorial island — opening scene (auto-plays at the family rocks)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tut.intro.1 = Ma Duiker: Jan! There you are. The morning dive's done - the others are up on the rocks drying their wings.
tut.intro.2 = Ma Duiker: Ag, don't sulk. So your wings won't dry and you sink like a stone. You're MY stone, and that's the end of it.
tut.intro.3 = Ma Duiker: Now - something big washed up on the north beach at dawn. Black and white, and it MOVES. Go and see. Careful, hey!
tut.intro.4 = (Touch the screen and drag - Jan waddles the way you pull. Head north along the beach.)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tutorial island — Ryno's conversation stages
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tut.ryno.meet.1 = ???: Haai! Another one! I KNEW it - I told the colony I smelled penguin on this wind.
tut.ryno.meet.2 = Jan: Penguin? No, no. I'm a cormorant. A bad one. My wings never dry, I can't fly, and when I dive I just... sink.
tut.ryno.meet.3 = Ryno: Boet. Look at me. Now look at you. Now look at your family. You and I are penguins.
tut.ryno.meet.4 = Ryno: Years back a hen from our colony, Annika, swam out past the shipping lane after sardine. A storm rolled in and sat for a week. She never came home.
tut.ryno.meet.5 = Ryno: She was carrying an egg when she left. You have her eyes, boet. I'd swear it on my last pilchard.
tut.ryno.meet.6 = Jan: ...Ma always said the storm brought me in.
tut.ryno.meet.7 = Ryno: Then it's settled. And listen: penguins don't fly through the air. We fly UNDERWATER. Talk to me again when you're ready for your first lesson.

tut.ryno.swim.1 = Ryno: Lesson one. The water isn't your enemy - it's your sky. Head down, feet back, and POINT yourself somewhere.
tut.ryno.swim.2 = Ryno: And take these - shell fragments off the tide line. The sea grinds their edges knife-sharp. Flung right, an edge like that slices kelp, rope, whatever needs cutting.
tut.ryno.swim.3 = (Ryno's ShellThrow is now equipped as one of Jan's item attacks.)
tut.ryno.swim.4 = Ryno: See the stone ring off the east shore? An old fish-trap ruin. The cove between here and there is calm - and something glints inside that ring.
tut.ryno.swim.5 = Ryno: Storm-kelp is choking the gap in the ruin's wall. Swim over and fling a shell through it - only an edge cuts kelp, boet. Beaks and flippers just bounce off.
tut.ryno.swim.6 = Ryno: Follow me, boet - it's a waddle down the shore to the cove. Keep up with a penguin on a mission!

tut.ryno.remind.1 = Ryno: In you go, boet - the water's right here. Slash the kelp, and see what the sea left you in that ring.

tut.ryno.gull.1 = Ryno: A fishing hook! Lekker. Sailors lose them by the dozen - hooked under a flipper, that point stabs deeper than any beak.
tut.ryno.gull.2 = Ryno: Put it to work - that fat kelp gull is back at your family's fish pens, beak in the catch. It's strutting around the south shore. Chase it off.
tut.ryno.gull.3 = Ryno: One more trick. A thief that's busy thieving never watches its tail. Come up quiet BEHIND it, and the first klap is free - before it even knows there's a fight.
tut.ryno.gull.4 = (Sneak attack: stand directly behind an unaware enemy and a mark pulses on it - tap to strike first. Works up close with melee, or from a few tiles back with a ranged weapon.)
tut.ryno.gull.5 = (Equip first: tap the round menu button in the corner, open the bag, and slot the FishingHook into an item-attack slot.)
tut.ryno.gull.6 = (Then walk up to the gull - or sneak in behind it - to start the fight. In battle: pick a move, then a target - FishingHook up close, ShellThrow from a distance.)
tut.ryno.gull.7 = Ryno: Follow me south, boet - stay close now. I'll take the dune above the pens. Quiet feet, remember.

tut.ryno.ranged.1 = Ryno: You klapped it! Ha! But listen, boet - a kelp gull never loses alone. It sulks on the water a while, then comes back with cousins. They ALWAYS come back with cousins.
tut.ryno.ranged.2 = Ryno: So, next lesson. When a mob lands on you, don't waddle into the middle of it. A Tackle only reaches the one right at your beak.
tut.ryno.ranged.3 = (Melee moves like Tackle and FishingHook only hit an enemy directly ahead of you. Ranged moves like ShellThrow can hit ANY enemy, wherever they stand.)
tut.ryno.ranged.4 = Ryno: Knock the far ones down with shells, and Tackle whatever's rude enough to get close. Fight the whole flock, boet, not one bird at a time.
tut.ryno.ranged.5 = Ryno: And don't forget your quiet trick - it works with shells too. Line one up from BEHIND, two or three paces back, and the first bird's down before the brawl even starts.
tut.ryno.ranged.6 = Ryno: Look for the fat one standing dead still, eyes locked on the pens. Too greedy to watch its own tail. Creep in behind THAT one first, hey.
tut.ryno.ranged.7 = Ryno: And if they spot you and give chase - don't be proud, boet. RUN. Gulls are greedy but lazy: lure one away from its cousins, then turn and klap it on its own.
tut.ryno.ranged.8 = Ryno: ...You hear that skreeing? South side. THE PENS, BOET! GO!

tut.ryno.raidremind.1 = Ryno: The pens, boet! Three of them! Shells for the far ones, Tackle for the brave ones - GO!

tut.ryno.finale.1 = Jan: Ryno... if I'm a penguin, where is everyone? You're the first one I've ever seen.
tut.ryno.finale.2 = Ryno: That's the sore truth, boet. There isn't enough fish left to keep a colony together. Every season we swim further from home just to eat.
tut.ryno.finale.3 = Ryno: Great steel ships from across the ocean - whole fleets of them - drag nets wider than this island. They scrape the sea bare and haul it all over the horizon.
tut.ryno.finale.4 = Jan: They can't just TAKE the whole sea. Somebody has to fight back.
tut.ryno.finale.5 = Ryno: Ha! Annika's egg, no mistake. There's a village up the coast where the fed-up are gathering - penguins, seals, all of us. They could use a fighter like you.
tut.ryno.finale.6 = Ryno: And I'll take you there myself, boet - the channel north is a short swim, and my wake is easy to follow.
tut.ryno.finale.7 = Ryno: But family is family. Go say your goodbyes properly - all of them. I'll wait by the water till you're ready.

tut.ryno.waitfam.1 = Ryno: No rush, boet. Goodbyes are a thing you only get one of. Ma, Pa, the little one - then come find me.

tut.ryno.waitnest.1 = Ryno: Something still pulling at you, boet? Ja - the west point, Ma said. Go stand in it once. We leave when your heart's packed, not just your bag.

tut.ryno.leave.1 = Ryno: Goodbyes said? Good man. Then it's time - the colony's waiting, and so is your fight.
tut.ryno.leave.2 = Ryno: ...What's that under your wing? ...Ja, boet. That's hers. That's Annika's. Bring it home.
tut.ryno.leave.3 = Ryno: Stay close to my wake and swim steady. The channel's calm today - the sea knows a big day when it sees one.
tut.ryno.leave.4 = (Ryno dives in and arrows north under the water. The channel is open - follow him across, then up the sand to the exit.)

tut.ryno.done.1 = Ryno: Through here, boet. The colony's a long way up the coast - days of swimming. Good thing you've got a guide, hey?

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tutorial island — the cormorant family
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tut.ma.base.1 = Ma Duiker: North beach, love. Big black-and-white thing, flopped up with the tide. Probably harmless. Probably.
tut.ma.base.2 = Ma Duiker: And stay off the deep water. You know how you get.
tut.pa.base.1 = Pa Duiker: Wind's from the west again. Fish are thin this season.
tut.pa.base.2 = Pa Duiker: Thinner every year, if you ask me. Nobody asks me.
tut.sib.base.1 = Vlerkie: I dove twelve fathoms today! Bet you ca- oh. Sorry, Jan.
tut.sib.base.2 = Vlerkie: ...I like your waddle, though. It's a good waddle.

tut.family.proud.1 = Ma Duiker: You chased that thieving gull off! Come here, let me look at you. My little fighter.
tut.family.proud.2 = Pa Duiker: The pens are quiet for the first time in weeks. Well done, my boy.

tut.family.raid.1 = Ma Duiker: Jan! The whole mob's come back for the pens - a week of herding, gone in an afternoon if they gut them!
tut.family.raid.2 = Pa Duiker: Three of the buggers this time! Watch the sky, my boy!
tut.family.raid.3 = Vlerkie: I threw a pebble and missed! Get them, Jan!

tut.family.proud2.1 = Ma Duiker: Three at once! I watched the whole thing with my heart in my beak. Look at you. LOOK at you!
tut.family.proud2.2 = Pa Duiker: First quiet the pens have had all season. That was proper fighting, son.

# Farewells — one scripted goodbye per family member, all three required
# before Ryno opens the channel. The .after lines play on re-talk.
tut.ma.farewell.1 = Ma Duiker: A whole village of penguins, hey. So the sea sent you, and now the sea wants you back.
tut.ma.farewell.2 = Ma Duiker: You listen to me, Jan Duiker. You were never a bad cormorant. You were always a lekker penguin. MY penguin. That doesn't stop at the waterline.
tut.ma.farewell.3 = Ma Duiker: Here - sardines for the crossing. Don't argue with your mother. (Ma tucks three sardines under your wing.)
tut.ma.farewell.4 = Ma Duiker: And Jan... before you cross, go up the west point rock. Where the tide first gave you to me. There's something up there that's yours.
tut.ma.after.1 = Ma Duiker: Go on now, before I change my mind and sit on you like an egg.

tut.pa.farewell.1 = Pa Duiker: The storm brought you in. Suppose the sea's calling you back. That's the way of tides.
tut.pa.farewell.2 = Pa Duiker: I never worried about you, boy. Wings dry or wet, you always came up with something. ...Ag. Maybe I worried a little.
tut.pa.farewell.3 = Pa Duiker: Swim straight, Jan. And if you meet those trawlers - give them hell from the Duikers.
tut.pa.after.1 = Pa Duiker: Wind's turning. Good crossing weather. Off you go.

tut.sib.farewell.1 = Vlerkie: You're really going? To a whole COLONY of penguins who all swim like you?
tut.sib.farewell.2 = Vlerkie: ...I'm going to miss losing races to you. That's a joke. I always win. ...It's less fun than I thought it would be.
tut.sib.farewell.3 = Vlerkie: Bring me something from the mainland! And peck a trawler for me! TWO trawlers!
tut.sib.after.1 = Vlerkie: When I can dive twenty fathoms I'm coming to visit. Count on it!

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tutorial island — kelp blockage, gull, rescue, objectives
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tut.kelp.cut.1 = Jan flings a shell edge-first into the tangle - once, twice. The storm-kelp parts like old rope.
tut.kelp.cut.2 = That felt... natural. Like something a penguin was built to do.
tut.kelp.blocked.1 = A dense tangle of storm-kelp chokes the gap in the old wall. Too tough to pull apart with flippers - it needs a cutting edge, not a poke.

tut.cache.equip = (Equip it before the fight: tap the round menu button in the corner, open the bag, and slot the FishingHook into an item-attack slot.)

tut.gull.victory = The gull flaps off over the water, screeching insults. Ryno will want to hear about this.
tut.raid.victory = The mob scatters over the swells, screeching. The fish pens - and the family's catch - are safe.

tut.rescue.1 = Ma Duiker hauls you out of the surf by the scruff of your neck. "Enough heroics for one tide, my boy."
tut.rescue.2 = Catch your breath, then try again. That gull has it coming.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tutorial island — dressing: tide pools, buoy dare, storm-nest, crate, decor
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tut.pool.catch = A sardine, stranded by the ebbing tide, flicks in the shallow pool. Jan tips it into his bag before it can argue.
tut.pool.hint = (Food heals. Open the bag from the round corner button and eat a sardine when your health runs low - in battle it costs a turn, so snack smart.)
tut.pool.empty = The pool is empty. The next tide will bring something new.
tut.pool.full = Jan's food bag is full. The sardine flips back into the pool, looking smug about it.

tut.buoy.early = An old bell buoy, rust-streaked and listing, moored out in the cove. It clongs softly with the swell.
tut.buoy.clong = Jan slaps a flipper against the old buoy. CLONG. The sound rolls across the whole cove. Vlerkie definitely heard that.
tut.buoy.again = Jan pats the buoy. Clong. Old friends now.

tut.sib.dare.1 = Vlerkie: So the penguin man taught you to swim, hey? Then prove it. The old bell buoy out in the east cove - touch it and come tell me. I dare you.
tut.sib.dare.2 = Vlerkie: What? I'd do it myself, obviously. I'm just... busy. Drying my wings. GO ON then.
tut.sib.remind.1 = Vlerkie: The bell buoy, Jan! East cove! Touched it yet, or are you scared of a floating pot?
tut.sib.darewin.1 = Vlerkie: You ACTUALLY touched it?! I heard the clong from HERE! Okay. Okay okay okay. Here - two sardines from my secret stash. A deal's a deal.
tut.sib.darewin.2 = Vlerkie: (Don't tell Ma about the secret stash.)

tut.nest.early = An old ring of driftwood on the high rock, silvered by storms. Something about it makes Jan's chest go tight. Ma would know.
tut.nest.1 = A ring of storm-driftwood, packed tight with old feathers, high above the water. This is where Ma found you - the nest the sea built out of a wreck and a gale.
tut.nest.2 = Wedged deep in the weave, kept dry by seventeen winters: one long feather. Black above, white below. Penguin.
tut.nest.3 = Jan tucks Annika's feather under his wing, next to Ma's sardines. Somewhere north, a colony is waiting for both of them.
tut.nest.after = The empty nest holds the shape of the wind. Jan carries the rest of it with him now.

tut.crate.1 = A splintered crate, half-buried in the sand. The boards are stamped with letters from no alphabet Jan knows.
tut.crate.2 = Inside: a torn scrap of netting, mesh fine as feathers. Whatever this net was made to catch, it wasn't made to let anything go.

tut.pen.full = A ring of stacked stones holds back a pocket of sea. Inside, the morning's catch circles silver - herded in at high tide, kept fresh for the lean days. The gulls know it too.
tut.pen.safe = The penned fish circle their stone ring, calm and unbothered. Safe - for now, and thanks to Jan.

tut.decor.driftwood = A silver-grey driftwood log, sanded smooth by a hundred tides. Warm from the sun. A very good log.
tut.decor.shells = A drift of broken shells, heaped up by the last spring tide. None of them the right shape for throwing.
tut.decor.stones = Someone has stacked five flat stones, biggest to smallest. Vlerkie's work. He calls it "art".

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tutorial island — neighbors
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tut.karel.base.1 = Oom Karel: In my day the shoals ran so thick you could walk to the mainland on their backs. Now? Lights on the horizon every night, and every morning the sea's a little emptier.
tut.karel.base.2 = Oom Karel: Big steel boats, boy. They don't fish. They HARVEST. You mark old Karel's words.
tut.bettie.base.1 = Tannie Bettie: That black-and-white fellow on the north beach has been asking after you, skattie. Handsome, in a round sort of way.
tut.bettie.base.2 = Tannie Bettie: Your ma hasn't stopped watching the water since you started swimming. Don't you dare make her regret it.

tut.obj.move = Touch and drag - Jan waddles the way you pull
tut.obj.find = Find what washed up on the north beach
tut.obj.talk = Talk to Ryno again
tut.obj.kelp = Swim the east cove and slash the kelp at the ruin
tut.obj.cache = Search the ruin for what the sea left behind
tut.obj.shells = Show Ryno what the sea left you in the ruin
tut.obj.gull = Chase the gull off the fish pens on the south shore
tut.obj.report = Tell Ryno about the gull
tut.obj.raid = Drive the gull mob off the fish pens
tut.obj.report2 = Tell Ryno the pens are safe
tut.obj.farewell = Say goodbye to Ma, Pa, and Vlerkie
tut.obj.nest = Visit the west point rock before you leave
tut.obj.ready = Tell Ryno you're ready to go
tut.obj.leave = Swim the north channel and head for the mainland exit

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The journey north — plays once, on first arrival at the village hub
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tut.journey.1 = They swim north until the cormorant island is a smudge, then a memory. Strange beaches. Cold currents. Ryno knows every one by name.
tut.journey.2 = Days pass. Past headlands, past the hulks of old wrecks, sleeping in kelp so the current can't steal them. Jan's flippers ache, then harden.
tut.journey.3 = "Now you're swimming like a penguin," Ryno says one grey morning. And then: woodsmoke. Dock-creak. Voices. The village.
tut.journey.4 = Ryno: Told you I'd get you here, boet. Come - there's a whole harbor of the fed-up waiting to meet Annika's seun.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Defeat rescue — village
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
rescue.village.1 = We found you floating in the water and carried you back to the village.
rescue.village.2 = You're safe. Rest up, gather your courage, and head back when you're ready.
rescue.loss.both = In the swim back, you lost %d item(s) from your bag and %d weapon(s) took a beating.
rescue.loss.items = In the swim back, you lost %d item(s) from your bag.
rescue.loss.weapons = In the swim back, %d weapon(s) in your bag took a beating.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Village hub — Ryno between fishing runs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
hub.ryno.greet.1 = Ryno: There he is! Look at this place, boet - huts, a forge, a food bank. Barnacle by barnacle, the fed-up are building something.
hub.ryno.greet.2 = Ryno: Me? I'm for the deep water. A penguin's got to fish, and the shoals out past the point are still honest. Somebody has to keep this village in sardines.
hub.ryno.greet.3 = Ryno: Go find the elder - get yourself useful. I'll be around, boet. You can't lose me. Family, remember?
hub.ryno.later.1 = Ryno: Tide's not right yet, so you're stuck with me a while longer. Go on - this village won't explore itself.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Harbor floor 1
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
harbor.elder.1 = Jan! The sailors have taken all the fish!
harbor.elder.2 = You must fight them off. Be brave, little one.

harbor.clear.1 = The dock is clear! You've done well, Jan.
harbor.clear.2 = Rumor is more sailors are stalking the tidal pools further up the coast...
harbor.clear.3 = Don't stop here - press on up the coast. There's more waiting for you.

harbor.post.greet.1 = Jan! You did it - the sailors are gone!
harbor.post.greet.2 = The harbor is ours again. Fish for everyone tonight.
harbor.post.dock = Look at this dock! You can actually walk it end to end.
harbor.post.cache = Captain's cache fed the whole village. Bless you, Jan.
harbor.post.sealfree.1 = Arf! Thanks for cracking the Captain - he kept me chained below.
harbor.post.sealfree.2 = Mind if I tag along now? I've got scores to settle.
harbor.post.sealflavor = Arf! (A seal waddles past, belly full of sardines.)
harbor.post.swim.1 = Ahh! The water's perfect.
harbor.post.swim.2 = First swim since the sailors came. Feels like home.
harbor.post.swim.3 = Caught a sardine with my bare flippers! Ha!
harbor.post.swim.4 = Chk-chk-chk! (A chick dives under and comes back up giggling.)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Seal (captive rescue + recruitment)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
seal.captive = Arf! Let's teach those sailors a lesson together!
seal.mmph = ...mmph! (He's tied up. Defeat the sailors guarding him!)
seal.join.1 = Arf! Thanks for the rescue - let's teach them a lesson!
seal.join.2 = The seal joins your party. (XP is now split evenly.)
seal.full = Arf! Your party is full already.
seal.greet = Arf! Thanks for the rescue! %s joins your party.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Village hub NPCs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
hub.elder.1 = Welcome to the village, Jan.
hub.elder.2 = The sailors have moved up the coast. The harbor is through the south gate.
hub.elder.3 = Rest here whenever you need to. You'll always find your way back.

hub.smith.locked.1 = The blacksmith is hunched over a cold forge, shaping nothing in particular.
hub.smith.locked.2 = "Forge's cold. Nothing worth shaping 'til the harbor's ours again. Clear it and we'll talk."

scribe.ok.1 = I've recorded your journey in the village log.
scribe.ok.2 = Rest easy - you can pick up here next time.
scribe.fail.1 = My quill slipped - the log wouldn't take.
scribe.fail.2 = Come see me again in a moment.

keeper.ask = I'm collecting %s - bring me %d and I'll trade you something nice.
keeper.progress = (You have %d of %d.)
keeper.thanks = Excellent! That's just what I needed.
keeper.reward = Take this %s and %d %s for your trouble.
keeper.bagfull_food = (Your food bag is full too - some of the reward couldn't fit.)
keeper.bagfull = (Your bag was full - some of the reward couldn't fit.)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lore — logbooks & etchings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
lore.f2cave.title = Cave Etching
lore.f2cave.1 = An etching, scratched into the cave wall.
lore.f2cave.2 = "In the time before sails, the colony was the harbour. We dove with the seals, and the seals dove with us."
lore.f2cave.3 = Below the words, a faint outline of a flipper and a fin, side by side.

lore.f4trader.title = Trader's Ledger
lore.f4trader.1 = A clipped page from a scrap-trader's ledger, tacked to a beam.
lore.f4trader.2 = "Bring me what the sea coughs up. Hooks, shells, urchin spikes - I will take them off your flippers and call it square."
lore.f4trader.3 = "Do not bring rust. The forge will not eat rust."

lore.f5tally.title = Tally Mark
lore.f5tally.1 = A tally mark in damp ink, crossed out and re-drawn three times.
lore.f5tally.2 = "Three lanterns guide the captain's ship to dock. No light, no plank."

lore.f6log3.title = Captain's Log p.3
lore.f6log3.1 = A salt-stained page tucked under a crate.
lore.f6log3.2 = Captain's Log, page 3:
lore.f6log3.3 = "The penguins watch us from the rocks. They think we cannot see them counting."
lore.f6log3.4 = "Let them count. The hold is full and the tide is ours."

lore.f7log4.title = Captain's Log (Last)
lore.f7log4.1 = Captain's Log, final page.
lore.f7log4.2 = "All three dock lanterns are burning. I did not light them."
lore.f7log4.3 = "Something is climbing the gangplank."
lore.f7log4.4 = "If you are reading this and you are not me - leave my ship."

